      "Saint Ignatius of Constantinople": 1,
      "Ignatius, born Nicetas about 799, was the son of Emperor Michael I. After his father was deposed he was shut in a monastery, where he embraced the religious life and became an abbot. In 847 he became Patriarch of Constantinople. He refused to help force the empress Theodora into a convent and rebuked the Caesar Bardas for repudiating his wife, and Bardas had him sent into exile. Restored in 867, he served about ten more years and died on October 23, 877.": 1,
      "Brief story based on the Catholic Encyclopedia.": 1,
